            <div xml:id="d917">

                <pb facs="1025" n="881" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.7961/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-19T19:00:00-05:00">February 19, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Department’s 16, February 16, 7 p.m. I have before me copy of telegram from
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs to Olaya authorizing him to sign as desired by the
                    Department with one slight addition after words Colombian ports “where there are
                    authorities charged with carrying out the pertinent regulations.”</p>
                <pb facs="1026" n="882" xml:id="pg882"/>
                <p>Olaya authorized to annex as Colombian regulations of [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >sic</hi>] the “exact copy” of those presented by the Department as “at
                    present we have no especial legislation on the subject.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
